                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Braking force does work over a distance to remove the car's KE. Since KE = 0.5mv² and work done = F x d, we get d = KE / F = 0.5mv² / F. Because KE depends on v², the braking distance d is also proportional to v². Doubling speed quadruples KE, so the braking distance also quadruples for the same braking force.",
                    "marks": [
